# StarSim: Version & Three-Way Coordination Rule

## Core rule

**Exe, webpage (dist/), and desktop shortcut must ALWAYS be the same version.** Single canonical location: `dist-electron/StarSim.exe`. Web serves from `dist/`. Shortcut points to canonical exe only.

## Single source of truth

| Output | Location | Notes |
|--------|----------|-------|
| **Webpage** | `dist/` | Served by `npm run serve:web`; same bundle as exe |
| **Exe** | `dist-electron/StarSim.exe` | Canonical. Copied from win-unpacked; never use win-unpacked for shortcut |
| **Desktop shortcut** | `Desktop/StarSim.lnk` | MUST point to `dist-electron\StarSim.exe` only |
| **BUILD_ID.txt** | `dist/` and `dist-electron/` | Same timestamp = same version |

## Triggers (run full build)

- **Version bump** or **code changes**
- Run `npm run build:all` at the end of any session that modifies the app

## Sync pipeline

`npm run build:all` → npm install → clean → **web build** → **BUILD_ID** written → **electron-builder** (no rebuild) → copy to dist-electron → **shortcut** (canonical only)

## Verification

`npm run check-sync` — verifies BUILD_ID match, shortcut targets canonical exe (not win-unpacked).

## When sync fails

1. Close StarSim.exe, run `npm run build:all` with full permissions
2. If shortcut points to win-unpacked: run `npm run shortcut`
3. Never deliver without a complete coordinated build
